        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:34:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 750,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 580,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115036,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 173,
        "headingId": 580,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:34:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 751,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 581,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115037,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 173,
        "headingId": 581,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>About 10% of osteoblastomas are found in the craniofacial bones, most often in the body of the mandible. They may be intraosseous or periosteal {16129654}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:34:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 752,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 582,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115038,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 173,
        "headingId": 582,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Osteoblastoma may be asymptomatic or present with localized swelling and pain {17052641}.</p>\r\n<h5>Imaging</h5>\r\n<p>Radiographs show a circumscribed round to oval lesion &ge;&nbsp;20 mm in diameter, varying from radiolucent to radiopaque, and usually without a sclerotic border or periosteal reaction {17052641}. The clinical and radiological appearance is sometimes more aggressive and may mimic malignancy {21181315}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:34:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 753,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 583,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115039,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 173,
        "headingId": 583,
        "headingText": "<p >Osteoblastoma is a rare tumour that occurs mostly in the second to third decades of life, with a slight female predominance (unlike long bone lesions) {17052641}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-11-10T17:55:36"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 754,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 584,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115040,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 173,
        "headingId": 584,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:34:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 755,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 585,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115041,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 173,
        "headingId": 585,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Recurrent rearrangements of <em>FOS</em> or (less frequently) <em>FOSB</em> define osteoblastoma and osteoid osteoma {29858576} and are also found in cementoblastoma, suggesting a pathogenetic relationship {33653978}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:34:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 762,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 592,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115042,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 173,
        "headingId": 592,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Curettings show red to tan tissue, reflecting vascularity. If resected, bone expansion with well-defined borders is typical {8119712}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:34:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 756,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 586,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115043,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 173,
        "headingId": 586,
        "headingText": "<p>Osteoblastoma is composed of anastomosing trabeculae of bone and osteoid, rimmed by plump osteoblasts, sometimes with densely mineralized foci, and set in a loose, richly vascular fibrous stroma. Mitoses are rare {16129654}. A lack of nuclear atypia, permeative growth into surrounding bone, and atypical mitoses distinguish osteoblastoma from osteosarcoma {8119712}. In some cases, the osteoblasts may appear larger and epithelioid, but this does not indicate a clinically aggressive course. A tumour size of &gt;&nbsp;40&nbsp;mm and an anatomical site that makes removal difficult are better predictors of aggressive clinical behaviour {21181315; 25409851}.</p>\r\n<h5>Differential diagnosis</h5>\r\n<p>The differential diagnosis includes osteoid osteoma for a lesion &lt;&nbsp;20&nbsp;mm in diameter and cementoblastoma if on a tooth root.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2024-01-10T12:46:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 757,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 587,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115044,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 173,
        "headingId": 587,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:34:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 758,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 588,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115045,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 173,
        "headingId": 588,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The translocations of <em>FOS</em> and <em>FOSB</em> identified in osteoblastoma are extremely rare in osteosarcoma, and FOS immunohistochemistry may be a helpful diagnostic tool in this setting, but only if there has been short decalcification {31768625}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:34:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 761,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 591,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115046,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 173,
        "headingId": 591,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> a radiologically well-demarcated tumour; &ge;&nbsp;20&nbsp;mm diameter; bone tumour with trabeculae of woven bone; prominent plump osteoblasts; vascular stroma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:34:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 759,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 589,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115047,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 173,
        "headingId": 589,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:34:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 760,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 590,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115048,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 173,
        "headingId": 590,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Recurrence may follow curettage or incomplete removal {25409851}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:34:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]